Tyrennius.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Space Marine]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
[[Image:Ancient Tyrennius.jpg|thumb|300px|right|Ancient {{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1}}]]
Tyrennius was a [[Terran]], inducted into the Legion from the '''Midafrik Hive''' levies towards the end of the [[Unification War]], in preparation for the [[Great Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

He went on to serve in the earliest decades of the Great Crusade, before he was given command of his Legion's forces in the [[First Magellan Expedition]]. However, the Expedition ended in failure and Tyrennius was among the few to return from that doomed endeavor, though he had sustained such terrible wounds that only interment within a [[Contemptor Dreadnought]] saved him from death.{{Fn|1}}

Afterwards, he would continue to serve in the Ultramarines' [[8th Chapter (Ultramarines Legion)|Eighth Chapter]], fighting in [[The Calth Configuration]] for ten years, so by the time the [[Battle for Calth]] began, the Dreadnought was known as '''Ancient Tyrennius of the 8th Chapter''' [[Dainhold Tertiary Muster]].{{Fn|1}}

During the battle against the [[Word Bearers]] Legion, Tyrennius fought with bitter resolve against the Traitors on [[Calth]]'s surface and was instrumental in the defeat of a large Word Bearers force that assaulted the gate of '''Arcology XVk'''. It is not known however, if he survived the Battle for Calth.{{Fn|1}}

