Tytonida Nebaszinar Falx.wikitext:
{{OrdoXenosPortal}}
{{ambig|subject=Ordo Xenos inquisitor|disambiguation=Falx}}
'''Tytonida Nebaszinar Falx''' is a [[Radical]] [[Ordo Xenos]] [[Lord Inquisitor]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
Before becoming an Inquisitor, Falx served as an [[acolyte]] on [[Inquisitor Kryptman]]s retinue.{{Fn|1b}}

In [[M42]], she journeyed into the murky depths of [[heresy]], by entering into a trading arrangement with the [[Ork]] [[Blood Axes]] interpreter [[Biter (Blood Axe)|Blood Axe]]. She was eager{{Fn|1a}} to find the answer of how the [[Warboss|Warlord]] [[Ghazghkull Thraka]]'s ascendance came to be{{Fn|2}} and agreed to pay the Greenskins' price of 120 [[Imperial]] weapons, of various sizes, and the location of 15 worlds the Blood Axes could safely raid{{Fn|1a}}. Many have lost their minds trying to unravel the mystery of Thraka's rise to power{{Fn|2}}, but after trading with the Greenskins{{Fn|1a}}, Falx now has in her custody the one creature in the universe who claims to know the truth of it all: The Warlord's [[Banner bearer]], [[Makari the Grot]].{{Fn|2}}

After hearing Makari's tale from Biter, the Ork was able to use his security clearance to alert an incoming armada. Falx attempts to flee with Makari in hand, but it is implied she was unable to escape from the Greenskins.{{Fn|1c}}

