Ughalax.wikitext:
{{BlackLegionPortal}}
'''Ughalax the Soul Eater''' is an infamous [[Black Legion]] [[Daemon Prince]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
In [[M42]], he became a commander of the [[Ark of Omen]] ''[[Unhallowed]]'' and launched an invasion of the [[Imperial]] world [[Vaingloria]], to claim the [[Key-Fragment]] it contained. As his forces fought across the world, Ughalax scorned the wider-conflict and led a hand picked [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] of Black Legionaries deep into [[Cadian]] lines, to secure the Fragment{{Fn|1a}}. Afterwards, the invasion continued and Ughalax later called upon the mightiest and most terrible [[Daemon|powers]] to aid in his final onslaught on the world.{{Fn|1b}}

Ughalax and his forces later reappeared on [[Arthas Moloch]], intent on claiming a key-fragment but coming into conflict with [[Commander Farsight]] and [[Orks]]. While failing to destroy the [[Tau]] or Orks, rival [[Alpha Legion]] agents under [[Lord Glass]] successfully acquired the Key-Fragment and offered it to the ''Unhallowed''s Warp Portal. Ughalax was not particularly angered by being denied glory, instead viewing himself as a cog in the machine of Chaos. He stated his forces had achieved their objective and ordered a withdrawal.{{Fn|2}}

Later, Ughalax's Ark of Omen ''Unhallowed'' was boarded by the combined armies of the [[Ork]] [[Warboss|Warlord]]s [[Bolgrog Bigtusk]], [[Skragga Fundastomp]], and [[Da Smoggboss]]. During the ensuing war, Ughalax was apparently killed, though none of the Orks can agree on who defeated the Daemon.{{Fn|3}}

