Uigui.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Uigui''' was a water-seller who lived on [[Baal Secundus]] around the time of the [[Devastation of Baal]].{{Fn|1a}}

At one time, Uigui's son, [[Teus]], attempted to become an [[Aspirant]] of the [[Blood Angels]].  Although Teus was a suitable genetic match to be considered for [[gene-seed]] implantation, he fell at the [[Place of Challenge]] and suffered a brain injury.{{Fn|1c}}  Although Teus survived, he was rejected and sent home with brain damage, which resulted in Uigui often abusing him as a failure.{{Fn|1a}}

Two years later{{Fn|1c}}, he was one of the many civilians drafted to defend the Blood Angels' [[fortress-monastery]] on [[Baal]] from the invading [[tyranid]]s of [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]].{{Fn|1b}}  He held the line alongside his son, with Teus saving Uigui's life more than once during the defence.  Ultimately, however, Uigui was mortally injured by a tyranid parasite organism.  As he lay dying, however, he saw his son become an [[Space Marine|angel]]: due to the losses sustained by the Sons of [[Sanguinius]], every compatable Baalite youth was to be inducted in one of the Chapters of the Blood and so Teus was recruited by a passing [[Sanguinary Priest]].{{Fn|1c}}

==Appearance==
As was typical for natives of Baal's moons, Uigui was disfigured by the radiation levels of the deserts.  As a result, he was hunched and ugly.  In addition, he had lost a finger to the reguliser [[Anton]] due to late payment of his debts.{{Fn|1a}}

