'''Ulfar''' was a member of the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]], who served in the [[Deathwatch]]'s [[Kill Team Primus]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Space Marine II}}
They were among the [[Imperial]] forces that defended{{Fn|1b}} the [[Recidious System]], after it was invaded by a [[Leviathan]] [[Splinter Fleet]].{{Fn|1c}} Kill Team Primus later answered{{Fn|1b}} [[Archmagos]] [[Nozick Beta-12]]'s plea for aid on [[Kadaku]], after the [[Xenos]] threatened the secretive [[Project Aurora]], that Nozick was developing. Because of the Archmagos' call for restrain in defending Kadaku, in order to prevent damaging the Project's facility,{{Fn|1a}} [[Kill Team Primus]] was charged with deploying a [[Virus Bomb]] to kill the [[Tyranids]].{{Fn|1b}} 

However the [[Kill-Team]]'s [[Corvus Blackstar]] was attacked by a swarm of [[Gargoyle]]s, as they neared the '''Orbital Launcher Facility''' that would be used to launch the [[Virus Bomb]]. In the battle that followed, the [[Black Templar]] [[Beren]] was able to hold onto the bomb, as most of [[Kill Team Primus]] was thrown from the gunship before it crashed. While he was able to remain with the gunship, though, the others were scattered in the area around the Facility. After they had fallen, only Ulfar and the [[Blood Angel]] [[Kelstros]] were able to make contact with each other. With time of the essence and not knowing the fate of their leader, the [[Deathwatch Black Shield|Black Shield]] [[Demetrian Titus]], Ulfar told Kelstros to take command. The Blood Angel then tasked the [[Space Wolf]] with recovering the Virus Bomb from the Blackstar's crash site, while he defended the Orbital Facility from the Tyranids. Ulfar would fight his through the [[Xenos]], but as he neared the gunship the Space Wolf was slain by a [[Tyranid Warrior]].{{Fn|1b}} 

This was seen by [[Demetrian Titus]], who had survived falling from their [[Corvus Blackstar]]. The crash, though, had damaged the [[Deathwatch Black Shield|Black Shield]]'s [[Vox]] equipment. While he was able to hear them, Titus had been unable to inform Ulfar and [[Kelstros]] that he still lived. By the time the Black Shield saw the [[Space Wolf]] die, Titus had recovered the [[Virus Bomb]] from [[Beren]]'s remains and had been making his way to the '''Orbital Launcher Facility'''. He vowed that Ulfar's death would not go unavenged and slew the Warrior. The Black Shield then made his way to the Facility, but by then Kelstros had been killed as well. Though he was now the only member of [[Kill Team Primus]] that still lived, Titus was able to successfully complete their mission.{{Fn|1b}}
