{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"Before becoming an [[Astartes]], I dreamed of becoming a [[skjald]], a keeper of stories. At feasts, I often sing of my brothers' exploits. Thousands are stored in my memory. When I am near, Wolves fight even more ferociously, for they know their deeds will be immortalised."'''''{{Fn|1}}}}
'''Ulfar''' is a member of the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]]. His pack - the [[Baleful Howl]] - was sent to the [[Koronus Expanse]] to quell a rise in [[Xenos]] and [[Chaos]] attacks at the behest of [[Lord Inquisitor]] [[Xavier Calcazar]].{{Fn|2a}}

==Biography==
===Pre-Astartes===
[[Image:Ulfar.jpeg|thumb|right|250px|Ulfar{{Fn|1}}]]
He was once a seafarer on [[Fenris]] and would go onto the '''Worldsea''' and slay [[Kraken]]s and [[Sea Drake]]s. When the '''Season of Fire''' would come, his ship would dock on '''Asaheim''' and battle for his clan's right to inhabit that land. He once dreamed of becoming a [[Skjald]], but after a great battle with [[Arnoolf Bloody Axe]], the [[Chooser of the Valiant]] deemed him worthy of becoming an Astartes.{{Fn|2b}}

He spent years in training before passing the [[Gate of Morkai]] and into the valley of dreams. Afterwards, the [[Rune Priest]]s found him without [[Corruption]] and he drank of the [[Cup of Wulfen]] and the [[Canis Helix]] transformed him. It cost him dearly, but he was able to recover from the bloodlust caused by the darkness of [[Wulfen]] and set out for [[The Fang]].{{Fn|2b}}

As a [[Neophyte]] he had to undergo a hunt. His was to face off with a [[Doppelgrendel]] where they fought for 5 days and nights. It was clever and would change its guise, but Ulfar defeated it and gouged its eye. The creature cursed him that he would never find an honourable death. When he returned, the [[Rune Priests]] imbued him with the remaining [[Gene-Seed]] and other organs.{{Fn|2b}}

===Astartes===
A marking on his armour of two crossed bones symbolizes a ''Mark of Endurance'' he earned when he sustained a serious injury from an [[Aeldari]] chieftain. The [[Wolf Priest]] said he would not survive, but after two years of delirium, he recovered. Later he hunted a blackmaned wolf and killed it with his bare hands, earning the rank of [[Wolf Guard]]. He wears the wolf fur on his shoulders. A claw-mark on his armour was made by [[Ragnar Blackmane|Jarl Ragnar]] when Ulfar beheaded the [[Archdespot of Tyranica II]]. He was blinded during the battle and hunted the sorcerer down by scent alone. He was also granted the accolade "Terminator" for other glorious victories.{{Fn|2b}}

His ambitions of becoming a [[Skjald]] had him remember the great exploits of his brothers, and they would fighter harder, knowing their deeds would be recorded. This earned him the moniker '''''Thunderlung''''' for his voice would know no fatigue whether fighting of feasting and could recite sagas or battle cries for hours. He became good friends with his former enemy [[Arnoolf Bloody Axe]] and they joined the [[Space Wolves]] at the same time. [[Skyaddi Twice-Thinker]] was a [[Rune Priest]], with thoughts enough for Arnoolf and Ulfar both. He taught Ulfar to compose verses.{{Fn|2b}}

===Koronus Expanse===
His 3-man squad was ambushed by [[Drukhari]] where he and his pack-brothers Arnoolf and Skyaddi were captured. They were taken to [[Commorragh]] to be tortured at the hands of the [[Drukhari]] [[Tervantias the Archmachinator]]. While Ulfar survived, Skyaddi was turned into an abomination and Arnoolf was tortured to death, leaving him as a [[Lone Wolf]]. {{Fn|2b}}

