Ulfreyr Ketilsson.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Ulfreyr Ketilsson''' is a [[Firstborn]] [[Space Wolves]] [[Wolf Priest]], who was sent as an envoy to the [[Wolfspear]] by his [[Wolf Lord]], [[Logan Grimnar]], to judge if the [[Ultima Founding]] [[Successor Chapter]] was worthy of being their kin.{{Fn|1}}
==History==
This was a similar task shared by a number of other [[Space Wolves]] and Ketilsson had judged several other [[Ultima Founding|Ultima]] [[Successor Chapters|Successors]], before he reached the [[Wolfspear]]. Upon reaching the [[Chapter]]'s [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]], [[108/Beta-Kalapus-9.2]], with the fleet he commanded, the [[Wolf Priest]] met with [[Chapter Master]] [[Senavael]]. Ketilsson was also accompanied by the Space Wolves [[Gjarmin]] and [[Troels]], who would serve as his councilors in the matter. Ketilsson told Senavael the reason for his arrival and then stated that on the orders of [[Logan Grimnar]], the three Space Wolves were to serve beside the Wolfspear until Ketilsson made his judgement. Senavael rejected this, though, claiming that the Wolf Priest's [[Wolf Lord]] had no authority over his Chapter. Ketilsson agreed that was true and told the Chapter Master they would leave, if the Wolfspear were not interested in being judged worthy of being kin to the Space Wolves.{{Fn|1}} 

Before the three could do so, however, [[Senavael]] stopped them. He then asked if the [[Wolfspear]] would be demeaned or judged harshly, as Ketilsson judged them. The [[Wolf Priest]] readily assured him, that was not what they had come to [[108/Beta-Kalapus-9.2]] to do. While the Wolfspear's worth was being considered, Ketilsson mainly sought to help impart the [[Space Wolves]]' heritage to their [[Successor Chapter]]. Upon hearing this, the [[Chapter Master]] agreed to allow the Wolf Priest to stay and make his decision. Ketilsson accepted this and then made the Wolfspear [[Bjarni Arvisson]] his intermediary to the Successor Chapter. The three Space Wolves and Arvission would then dine together and share knowledge about their respective Chapters to each other. Then as night fell on Beta-Kalapus, the Space Wolves fought beside the Wolfspear against the [[Daemon]]s that daily invaded their [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]]. It was as the two forces clashed, that Ketilsson decided the Wolfspear were worthy and contacted his fleet. Aboard it, was the large force of Space Wolves, the [[Wolf Lord]] [[Logan Grimnar]] had granted him to bestow upon the Wolfspear if they passed Ketilsson's judgment. At the Wolf Priest's command they deployed to Beta-Kalapus and arrived shortly after the invading Daemons were defeated. With these new reinforcements, the Wolfspear was brought to a full 1000 [[Space Marines]] and with his task now done, Ketilsson departed with his fleet shortly afterwards.{{Fn|1}}

