Ullis Temeter.wikitext:
{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was the [[Captain]] of the 4th Great Company of the [[Death Guard]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

Born on [[Terra]] as opposed to [[Barbarus]], Temeter often had tense relations with figures within the Legion such as [[Calas Typhon]] and [[Ignatius Grulgor]]. Temeter was ultimately sent by his own [[Primarch]] to the doomed world of [[Isstvan III]] as part of the loyalist contingent to be purged in preparation for the [[Horus Heresy]]. Warned of the betrayal by [[Saul Tarvitz]], Temeter directed as many of his men to a nearby sealed bunker to shelter from an imminent [[Virus Bomb]]. Despite urging from [[Huron-Fal]] he stubbornly refused to enter until all his soldiers were inside; he waited until the last possible second to order the bunker to be sealed, leaving no time for his own escape as the bombs fell. With Temeter blinded and their bodies dissolving, Fal carried his brother in his arms to a safe distance where they died together in the [[Dreadnought]]'s reactor explosion, rather than succumb to a death not of their choosing.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
