Ulrach Branthan.wikitext:
{{IronHandsPortal}}
[[Image:BranthanArt.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}} following his resurrection{{Fn|3a}}]]
'''Ulrach Branthan''' was the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[65th Clan-Company (Iron Hands)|65th Clan-Company]] of the [[Ninrakar Clan]] of the [[Iron Hands]] [[Legion]], who escaped from [[Istvaan V]] with a contingent of Iron Hands aboard the ''[[Sisypheum]]'' after having been seriously injured during the [[Drop Site Massacre]].{{Fn|1}}

Both of his legs had been mutilated as well as one of his arms and he suffered from multiple severe other wounds. When his damaged body was recovered and brought aboard the ''[[Sisypheum]]'' the [[Apothecary]] realised it was beyond repair. With no [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]]s available the Apothecary turned to the next option and used ''[[The Heart of Iron]]'', a relic from the [[Dark Age of Technology]]. This device clamped across the captain’s torso like a mechanised arachnid parasite and started to slowly regrow his damaged organs. But it was also feeding off his vitality and would most likely have killed him before healing all his damaged organs. In addition the [[stasis field]] generator of his medical casket helped to keep Branthan alive.{{Fn|1}}

Branthan was later revived inside the shell of the former [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] body of [[Karaashi Bombastus]] but without a sarcophagus, merely being placed into a cable-wound cocoon of raw sutures and bare flesh.{{Fn|2}} He took part in the final mission of the ''Sisypheum'' to acquire the [[Magna Mater]] on [[Luna]]. During the fighting, Branthan and [[Cadmus Tyro]] sacrificed themselves to hold off [[Justaerin]] in order to allow [[Nykona Sharrowkyn]] to escape with the Magna Mater.{{Fn|3b}}

