Umberco Eto.wikitext:
{{OrdoMalleusPortal}}
'''Umberco Eto, Questor of Tiarni Delta''', is a [[Thorian]] [[Psyker]] [[Inquisitor]] of the [[Ordo Malleus]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
His path to the Inquisition began when he was [[press-gang]]ed from his home world [[Arbrenia]] and forced to work for the [[Rogue Trader]] [[Daskon Holpstein]] aboard his ship, the ''[[Prince Yugen]]''.{{Fn|1}}

Eto would serve Daskon for some time, before the Rogue Trader's activities drew the attention of Inquisitor [[Malordnu]], who quarantined the ''Prince Yugen'' and psychically tested all of the ship's crew. This led to the discovery of Eto's psychic potential and he was taken to a [[League of Black Ships|Black Ship]] for further evaluation. There, he was deemed worthy of being an asset to the Inquisition and Eto was then taken to the Inquisitorial fortress on [[Judgement (World)|Judgement]], where he eventually became the [[Interrogator]] of Inquisitor [[Coteaz]].{{Fn|1}}

Following his successful service with Coteaz, Eto became an Inquisitor in his own right and subsequently made his reputation by destroying a [[Daemon]]-worshiping [[Chaos Cult|Cult]] on the [[Imperial]] [[Asteroid|asteroid colony]] of [[Tiarni Delta]].{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
Eto carries trophies taken from his dead enemies. He also wields a [[psycannon]] and a [[Force Axe]], whose blade is shaped like a snarling tiger.{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*Umberco Eto may be named after Italian writer [[wikipedia:Umberto Eco|Umberto Eco]].

