Uradus.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}
'''Uradus''' was a [[Hawk Lords]] [[Stormtalon]] pilot, who was among the [[Chapter]]'s forces that served in [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus]]'s [[Battle Group Jovia]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
During the [[Indomitus Crusade]], he served in a [[Stormtalon]] squadron with his [[Hawk Lords]] [[Battle Brother]]s [[Armandus]], [[Voldwyn]] and [[Korr]] as part of [[Battle Group Jovia|Jovia]]'s '''Task Force IX'''.  It was sent by the Battle Group to reclaim the [[Imperial]] world [[Garvetha Primus]] and its [[system]] from [[Heretics]]. The Task Force invaded the world and soon only needed to conquer the city of '''Deng-Var''' to reclaim the planet once more. This would then allow the world's system to be opened up for further invasions.{{Fn|1}}

However, as they were fighting to take back the city, the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]] destroyed the [[Choral Engine]] on the world of [[Malakbael]] in the [[Imperium Nihilus]], which the majority of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus|Fleet Quartus]]' forces had been defending. The [[psychic]] beacon's subsequent explosion then unleashed [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]] [[Warp]] plague within Malakbael's [[Malak System|system]]. However, due to the Fleet's Battle Groups sharing psychic channels with each other, the Murder-Curse was able to spread to them all, no matter where they were located within the [[Galaxy]]. Because of this, the [[Warp]] plague soon reached '''Task Force IX''' and those who were infected by it immediately became servants of the [[Khorne|Blood God]]. Now filled with murderous bloodlust and rage, they fell upon anyone that was near them, including their former allies. While Uradus was able to resist the [[Murder-Curse]], [[Armandus]], [[Voldwyn]] and [[Korr]] all fell victim to it. The three infected pilots could somehow sense this though and within moments, Uradus' corrupted [[Battle Brother]]s shot him out of the sky.{{Fn|1}}  

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Arks of Omen: Angron]], pgs. 46-49 

