Vadok Singh.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Vadok Singh, the Warmason''', was an [[Imperial]] architect who aided the [[Primarch]] [[Dorn]] in turning the [[Imperial Palace]] into a fortress during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

He and Dorn often disagreed, while conversing on how best to prepare the Imperial Palace for the traitorous [[Warmaster]]'s invasion of [[Terra]], which irritated Singh — as he was an experienced craftsman, while Dorn was a warrior. This, combined with referring to the Primarch by his first name, Rogal, often irritated the accompanying [[Imperial Fists]] [[Space Marine Captain|Captains]] [[Sigismund]] and [[Archamus]]. As a result of this, on more than one occasion Dorn had to signal the two Captains to stand down, before they confronted Singh for his lack of respect towards their Primarch. Despite their differences, though, Singh and Dorn both vowed to work together to restore the Imperial Palace to its former splendor, once Horus' forces were defeated.{{Fn|1}}

Later in the Heresy, the formerly imprisoned [[Space Marine Legion|Legionary]] [[Severian (The Wolf)|Severian]] invaded Singh's private estate in his desperate attempt to flee from Terra. He kidnapped Singh and would have escaped with the Warmason aboard a shuttle, had the expert hunter [[Nagasena]], who had been charged with killing Severian, not appeared and defeated the Legionary. Though Singh was horribly shaken by the event, he was unharmed and continued to aid Dorn in fortifying the Imperial Palace{{Fn|2}}. After the Imperium succeeded in defeating Horus' forces, Singh was honoured for his work and his remains were later stored within the vast [[Warmason's Cathedral]] on [[Lubentina]]. The Cathedral was protected by the [[Battle Sisters]] of the [[Order of the Sombre Vow]], and it also contained Singh's possessions that were declared to be relics by the Imperium{{Fn|3a}}. One of which was the [[Warmason's Casket]], which was later sought out by a squadron of invading [[Iron Warriors]].{{Fn|3b}}

Because of his Masonic guild's gene-breeding their bloodline to favour height for the purpose of surveying and overseeing, Singh was taller than Dorn, but was also incredibly thin. Due to his station, Singh's guild supplied him with a number of slaves, which always followed in the Warmason's wake and saw to his needs.{{Fn|1}}

