{{IronWarriorsPortal}}
'''Vaen''' is an [[Iron Warriors]] [[Chaos Lord|Lord Admiral]] whose flagship, the ''[[Merciless Spite]]'', crash landed upon the [[Imperial]] [[Feudal World]] [[Prime Gala]]. The world had been colonized by the [[Knights]] of [[House Terryn]] and was ruled by [[High King]] [[Dontros]], who sent his forces to kill the invaders. However, when the Knights arrived, Vaen unleashed swarms of [[Heldrake]]s, which easily destroyed House Terryn's forces. Vaen then rebuilt the Knights and installed his favoured [[Chosen]] lieutenants to pilot them. With these corrupted Knights under his control, Vaen went on to lead his forces in a successful conquest of Prime Gala.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Chaos Space Marines (8th Edition)]], pg. 32 — ''The Machine Eyrie''
[[Category:Characters (Iron Warriors)]]

Vaer Greyloc.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Vaer Greyloc''' was a [[Jarl]] of the [[Space Wolves]]. Commander of the Space Wolves Twelfth [[Great Company]] in [[M32]], he oversaw the defenses of [[Fenris]] against the [[Thousand Sons]] in the [[Battle of the Fang]]. Though a skilled commander and powerful warrior, not even Greyloc could stand before the might of [[Magnus the Red]]. Towards the end of the battle, Magnus beat the Jarl to death with his bare hands in front of [[Bjorn]].{{Fn|1a}}

Although Bjorn was acclaimed for his valour during the battle, the venerable [[Dreadnought]] said that the true victory belonged to Greyloc, for his leadership and the awesome battle-fury that had enabled him to grievously wound the [[Daemon Primarch]], even if he could not defeat him.{{Fn|1b}}

