Veniston.wikitext:
{{ImperialNavyPortal}}
'''Veniston''' is an [[Imperial Navy]] [[Admiral]], who commands the [[Battleship]] ''[[Holy Dignity]]''.{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
In late [[M41]], Veniston had command of a small [[Imperial Navy]] fleet that was on an extended patrol. The fleet consisted of the [[Cruiser]] ''[[Divine Justice]]'' and its three [[Frigate]] escorts the ''[[Glorious]]'', the ''[[Apollo]]'' and the ''[[Excellent]]''. While the ''Divine'' was normally command by [[Imperial Navy Captain|Captain]] [[Kaurl]], it was under Veniston's control for the duration of the patrol. Under his command, the fleet engaged an [[Ork]] controlled [[Space Hulk]], that was destroyed by the ''Divine's'' fighter craft. This was at a heavy cost, though, and the fleet would continue on its patrol with under-strength fighter squadrons. However the rest of the patrol's duration saw them only fight against [[Pirate]]s and the occasional smuggler.{{Fn|1}}

A year and a half after destroying the Space Hulk, the fleet was able to resupply on [[Saltius]], where they received new orders. They were to join the Imperial Navy fleet that was fighting to reclaim [[Mearopyis]] from the [[Noctal]] species. When they arrived, though, the Navy's Sector Command placed Veniston in command of the entire fleet. He then replaced the recalled [[Admiral]] [[Kright]] and took command of the [[Battleship]] ''[[Holy Dignity]]''.{{Fn|1}}

