Verodan.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
{{Fanatic}}
'''Verodan''' was a venerable [[Wolf Priest]], in the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was serving under [[Force Commander]] [[Rakhim]], aboard the [[Pride of Fenris]], when they received a [[Operation Salvation|plea for aid]] from [[Asedor]]. Rakhim then led his forces to the [[Imperial]] [[Hive World]], but discovered that it was firmly in control of the [[Brothers of Retaliation]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] and their [[Chaos Cult]] and [[Traitor Guard|Traitor PDF]] allies. Seeing this, led the Commander to know that his forces were outnumbered and could not win in a direct assault against the invaders. Instead he sought to escort Asedor's [[Imperial Governor]], [[Elias An'Therosed]], to the Pride of Fenris, so the Governor could provide intelligence about the [[Chaos]] forces they would face. This would then allow the [[Space Wolves]] to know where to aim their attacks, in order to ensure they defeated the invaders. Verodan was then part of the rescue-team that Rakhim led to extract An-Therosed and it [[teleported]] to the Governor's besieged palace in the '''Arden Prime''' [[Hive]].{{Fn|1}} 

They found [[Elias An'Therosed|An'Therosed]] with his remaining loyal forces and were preparing to [[teleport]] back to the [[Pride of Fenris]], when disaster struck. The [[Brothers of Retaliation]] became aware of the [[Space Wolves]]' presence and jammed the rescue-team's teleport signal. This prevented them from escaping with An'Therosed and with [[Asedor]]'s orbital defenses in the [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]'s hands, the Pride of Fenris was also unable to send [[Thunderhawks]] to extract the Space Wolves and Governor. The Chaos invaders then attacked them, but An'Therosed informed the rescue-team that there was a prototype [[Escape Pod]], at the top of '''Arden Prime''''s [[Hive-spire]]. While it could not house all of them, the Escape Pod was made to be invisible to sensors and could safely reach the Pride of Fenris. But they would need to reach it before the Chaos invaders broke through their defensive lines. Acting quickly, the Space Wolves began escorting the Governor to the Escape Pod chamber, while leaving An'Therosed's remaining loyal Adeptus Arbites and Guardsmen to fended off the invaders. However the [[Chaos]] forces overran the Governor's forces and a group of the Brothers of Retaliation began pursing the rescue-team. The [[Chaos Space Marines]] were then able to catch up with the Space Wolves, as they neared the Escape Pod's chamber.{{Fn|1}} 

In the intense fighting that erupted, both sides suffered numerous losses and [[Rakhim]] sought to ensure that the [[Imperial Governor]] was safely extracted. He began escorting [[Elias An'Therosed|An'Therosed]] to the [[Escape Pod]] chamber, while Verodan and the '''Loki''' and '''Black Wolves''' packs, provided covering fire. However when [[Ajan]]'s [[Chaos Terminators]] neared the Governor's location, the [[Wolf Priest]] led the Black Wolves in a charge against them, to protect An'Therosed. The Space Wolves proved to be no match for the Chaos Terminators, though, and they were all killed except for a mortally wounded Verodan. The cackling Chaos Terminators then surrounded the Wolf Priest, but Verodan used the last of his strength to activate a [[Melta Bomb]]. The resulting explosion not only killed the Wolf Priest, but also Ajan and the Chaos Terminators as well.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
