Vesper Kith.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Vesper Kith, Dark Spear of Alaitoc''', is an [[Asuryani]] [[Farseer]] from the [[Craftworld]] [[Alaitoc]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
He was among{{Fn|1}} the [[Asuryani]] and [[Drukhari]] forces that invaded the [[Chinchare Subsector]] in the wake of the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]]. The [[Xenos]] sought to rebuild ancient monoliths located on many of the [[Subsector]]'s worlds in order to dissipate dangerous [[warp]] currents that were threatening the very fabric of the [[Webway]]. However the [[Imperium]] would later launch the [[Dark Crusade (Imperium)|Dark Crusade]]'s [[Kith Campaign]] against the invading Xenos.{{Fn|2}} The Campaign was named after Kith himself, as research on the various Asuryani and Drukhari in the Chinchare Subsector, led the Imperium to determine that the [[Farseer]] was a leader who posed a major threat to it.{{Fn|1}} During the course of the Campaign, Kith coordinated several attacks on Imperial worlds,{{Fn|3}} which included those upon [[Orthrea]]. These attackers were then investigated by the [[Ordo Xenos]] [[Interrogator]] [[Janus Dubois]], who served the [[High Inquisitor]] [[Geromius Staanberg]]. Dubois, though, would fail to find the purpose or pattern to the attacks.{{Fn|1}} While the Imperium later defeated and reaped a high cost in lives against the invading Asuryani and Drukhari, Kith was among those that survived the conflict.{{Fn|2}} 

