Videx.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
'''Videx''' is a [[Lector-Dogmatis]] of the [[Forge World]] [[Metalica]]. Videx is a zealous adherent to the [[Lex Mechanicus|tenets]] of the [[Cult Mechanicus]] and constantly warns against the potential corruption of conducting research into [[xenos]] artefacts.{{Fn|2a}}

==Silva Tenebris==
[[Image:Videx.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Videx]]
In the [[Era Indomitus]], Videx served as part of a triumvirate commanding an [[Ark Mechanicus]], the ''[[Caestus Metalican]]'', in a salvage expedition to [[Silva Tenebris]]. The triumvirate was made up of himself, [[Magos Dominus]] [[Faustinius]] of [[Mars]], and [[Acquisitor (Adeptus Mechanicus)|Tech-Acquisitor]] [[Scaevola]] of [[Stygies VIII]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2b}}

He was the mission's chief functionary of the Cult Mechanicus. His roles were to ensure that proper observations were made to keep the [[machine-spirit]]s honoured and uncorrupted, as well as watching over the spiritual health of the mission's personnel.{{Fn|2a}}

Part of Videx's fanaticism is due to him witnessing [[Siege of Hypnoth|the destruction]] of [[Forge World]] [[Hypnoth]], where Necrons released a technophagic virus that destroyed the Adeptus Mechanicus defences and ultimately led to the planet's dramatic fall. Videx is motivated by the horror and rage he felt from what he witnessed. To Videx, complete annihilation of the xenos is a just and logical response to what he witnessed on Hypnoth. Seeking to exact revenge on the Necron wherever possible. Videx is deeply suspicious of Scaevola and warned Faustinius to be wary of her motives.{{Fn|2a}}

Videx claimed that he elected to join the mission because Magos [[Rhesak]], like him, was from Metalica and the Forge World should be represented. In truth, Videx's real objective was to destroy the works of the alien anywhere he finds them, including the structures discovered on Silva Tenebris.{{Fn|2a}} His counsel of purging the Xenos threat in totality would eventually sway Magos Dominus Faustinius into executing [[Exterminatus]] upon the world.{{Fn|3}} After placing explosive charges around a vulnerable cluster of generators beneath the tomb of [[Neftusk]], Videx would summon several Metalican warship to rain down the Omnissiah's fury on the target. The explosion of the generators would cause a chain reaction within the world's crust and mantle resulting in the world tearing itself apart, being utterly obliterated.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
