Vogel (Rogue Trader).wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
{{Fanatic}}
'''Vogel''' is a [[Rogue Trader]].{{Fn|1a}} 
==History==
He is willing to find and sell [[Chaos]] artefacts to the highest bidder.{{Fn|1a}} Vogel also does business with [[Heretic]]s{{Fn|1b}} and [[Pirates]], even when he knows they will use his goods to do harm against the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|1c}} An example of this, is when Vogel attempted to destroy a [[Nuclear Weapon|tactical nuclear missile]] on an Imperial world, in order to ensure his dealings with [[heretics]] there were hidden from its authorities. However, this put him in conflict with [[Inquisitor]] [[Bell (Inquisitor)|Bell]], who sought to launch the nuke at the world's southern continent to destroy the Heretics instead.{{Fn|1b}} 

The two later clashed again, in the [[Imperial]] '''Vamhorn Stadium''', when Vogel sold an [[Archeotech]] shield generator to the [[Pirate]] leader [[Red Dog]]. This was despite knowing that Red Dog intended to use it to seal off and take control of the city the stadium was located in. But the [[Rogue Trader]] will not be paid by the Pirate leader, until the Archeotech was finished being installed in the stadium and was operational. As this is occurring, the shield generator is being watched over by Vogel's hired thug [[Krystis]], and several of Red Dog's pirates. [[Inquisitor]] [[Bell (Inquisitor)|Bell]] though, knows about the Pirate leader's plans and he is racing to stop the shield generator from being activated.{{Fn|1c}} 
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Vogel'', [[Bell (Inquisitor)|Bell]], [[Red Dog]] and [[Krystis]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Stephen Pearson]].{{Fn|1c}}

