Voldwyn.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}{{KhornePortal}}
'''Voldwyn''' is a [[Hawk Lords]] [[Stormtalon]] pilot, in [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus]]' [[Battle Group Jovia]] and is among its forces that have been corrupted by [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
During the [[Indomitus Crusade]], he served in a [[Stormtalon]] squadron with his [[Hawk Lords]] [[Battle Brother]]s [[Uradus]], [[Armandus]] and [[Korr]] as part of [[Battle Group Jovia|Jovia]]'s '''Task Force IX'''.  It was sent by the Battle Group to reclaim the [[Imperium Sanctus]] world [[Garvetha Primus]] and its [[system]] from [[Heretics]]. The Task Force invaded the world and soon only needed to conquer the city of '''Deng-Var''', to make Garvetha Primus' the [[Imperium]]'s once more. This would then allow the world's system to be opened up for further invasions. However it was as they were fighting to take back the city, that the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]] destroyed the [[Choral Engine]] on the [[Imperium Nihilus]] world [[Malakbael]], which the majority of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus|Fleet Quartus]]' forces had been defending. The [[psychic]] beacon's subsequent explosion, then unleashed [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]] [[Warp]] plague, within Malakbael's [[Malak System|system]]. However due to its Battle Groups sharing psychic channels with each other, the Murder-Curse was able to spread to them all, no matter where they were located within the [[Galaxy]].{{Fn|1}}  

Because of this, the [[Warp]] plague soon reached '''Task Force IX''' and those who were infected by it, immediately became servants of the [[Khorne|Blood God]]. Now filled with murderous bloodlust and rage, they fell upon anyone that was near them, including their former allies. While Voldwyn, [[Armandus]] and [[Korr]] all fell victim to it, [[Uradus]] was able to resist the [[Murder-Curse]]. The three infected pilots could somehow sense this though and within moments, Uradus' corrupted [[Battle Brother]]s shot him out of the sky. Armandus and Korr then instinctively formed up upon Voldwyn, as their pack began firing indiscriminately upon those fighting beneath them. At that time, Voldwyn's corrupted body began [[mutant|mutating]] and ropes of nerves and muscles emerged from cracks in his [[power armour]] to invade the instruments of Voldwyn's Stormtalon. Though Korr would be shot down shortly afterwards, the other two pilots continue to kill in Khorne's name.{{Fn|1}}  

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Arks of Omen: Angron]], pgs. 46-49 

