Vorchiss.wikitext:
{{TzeentchPortal}}
'''Vorchiss''' was a [[Chaos Sorcerer]] of [[Tzeentch]] who took part in the [[13th Black Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

While navigating one of the great ships of [[Ezekyle Abaddon|Abaddon's]] fleet, he felt the death cry of a mortal world echoing through the [[Warp]], another world that he knew had been slaughtered by the Despoiler. That sensation of death pushed Vorchiss, who had been a pawn of Chaos for ten thousand years, to his breaking point. He had felt his humanity slip away from him with the passing of each year he served the [[Chaos God]] Tzeentch, and he suddenly decided he could no longer walk the path of damnation. He looked upon the [[Astronomican|Light of the Emperor]] in the hope of redemption, and was rewarded with the strength to steer the vessel he was navigating into a raging Warp maelstrom. With his sacrifice, Vorchiss ensured that at least one host of monsters would not reach the [[Imperium]] world of [[Agripinaa]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
