Vorn Hagen.wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
'''Vorn Hagen''' was once the [[Chapter Master]] of the [[Imperial Fists]] and was well known for his precision of word and deed.{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Vorn Hagen was [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Imperial Fists]]' [[5th Company (Imperial Fists)|5th Company]]. Stern and resolute, he exemplified [[Rogal Dorn]]'s vision of a Space Marine. Hagen was notorious for his precision and disciplinary nature and saw artistry in war that few of his battle-brothers acknowledged. The only time a crack in his composure was seen was when he was confronted with recklessness on the part of his allies. It is said his favorite passage from the [[Book of Dorn]] concerned how a plan of a month's forging can be destroyed by a moment's blunder. Decades before his ascension as a mere [[Space Marine Scout|Scout]], Hagen closely studied the exploits of [[Darnath Lysander]] and as he rose through the ranks he secretly saw himself following in Lysander's footsteps.{{Fn|1a}}

Hagen fought alongside Lysander and [[Chapter Master]] [[Vladimir Pugh]] in the [[Infestation on Drashin]]. Hagen was promoted to [[Chapter Master]] after the death of Pugh in the battle; Lysander was the first choice, but refused the honor.{{Fn|1b}}

During the [[Invasion of Taladorn]], Hagen held exemplary command over half the Imperial Fists' companies, coming to lead the 5th as a part of the organization that followed Lysander's return.{{Fn|1a}}

Hagen later died [[Battle of Lion's Gate|defending Terra]] in the aftermath of the [[Great Rift]]'s creation and was succeeded by [[Gregor Dessian]].{{Fn|2}}

