Vykus Ordaris.wikitext:
{{RavenGuardPortal}}{{DeathwatchPortal}}
[[Image:VykusOrdaris.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Vykus Ordaris{{Fn|1b}}]]
'''Vykus Ordaris''' is a [[Raven Guard]] [[Deathwatch]] member of the [[Watch Fortress]] [[Keep Extremis]] and is part of [[Kill Team Mordelai]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He is a veteran [[Sniper]] specialist of few words, who possess an intimate knowledge of [[Xenos]] anatomy and infinite patience. Ordaris combines all of these abilities together, when the [[Raven Guard]] uses his [[Stalker Bolter]] to strike his foes in areas that will do the most harm. He has risen to become one of [[Keep Extremis]]' heroes and was present when the [[Great Rift]]'s creation placed the [[Watch Fortress]] within the [[Imperium Nihilus]]. This led it to become repeatedly attacked by [[Traitor]]s and Ordaris and his Deathwatch [[Battle Brothers]] successfully drove off all of the attacks. However in doing so, they suffered substantial casualties. Despite this, when Keep Extremis later received distress calls from [[Vigilus]], during the [[War of Beasts]],{{Fn|1b}} [[Watch Captain]] [[Tannister]] was sent to aid the [[Imperial]] world.{{Fn|1c}} He led a [[Watch Company]] aboard the [[Strike Cruiser]] [[Remorseless]] to Vigilus and it was in the process of forming the Company, that [[Watch Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Titus Mordelai]]'s [[Kill Team Mordelai]] was formed. It was composed of survivors of Keep Extremis' most badly mauled [[Kill-Team]]s and despite this, they formed a quick bond with each other. This was due to all of them losing comrades during the defense of their [[Watch Fortress]] and now having a desire to claim vengeance.{{Fn|1a}}  

By the time they reached [[Vigilus]], [[Kill Team Mordelai]] was ready to fight together.{{Fn|1a}} But as soon as the [[Strike Cruiser]] arrived there, the [[Remorseless]] received distress calls from across the [[Vigilus System]]. [[Watch Captain|Captain]] [[Tannister]] reacted to this new development by splitting his [[Watch Company]] into its individual [[Kill-Team]]s and sending them to answer each distress call. Kill Team Mordelai would not fight on Vigilus and was instead dispatched to aid the settlement of '''Vain Hope''' on [[Falsehood (World)|Falsehood]]. They deployed on the [[Death World]] via the [[Corvus Blackstar]] [[Alien's Bane (Corvus Blackstar)|Alien's Bane]] and sought to set up ambush points to attack the [[Drukhari]] that were raiding the settlement. This would be ruined, however, after the Kill Team was set upon by a giant creature known as a [[Carnivosaur]], which led a group of the invading Xenos to attack the Kill Team. They were able to defeat the Drukhari, though, and captured the only Xenos survivor of the group. After interrogating their prisoner, Kill Team Mordelai learned of the location for one of the Drukhari's encampments and destroyed it with the aid of Alien's Bane's firepower.{{Fn|1c}}

